252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (The phishing email detection and awareness assessment was carried out by following a particular approach to analyze the email samples and detect phishing attempts. The methodology was aimed at increasing cybersecurity awareness by reviewing publicly available phishing email samples. The methodology was based on ethical principles and allowed detecting phishing attempts by analyzing the phishing email samples without clicking on the links and opening attachments. Each step of the methodology was developed to ensure a safe analysis of the phishing email samples and prepare a phishing email detection report according to the industry standard.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (The first step in the methodology was to collect publicly available email samples that could represent the different categories of emails, such as Phishing, Suspicious, and Safe. In order to do that, the emails that could be used as examples of the Phishing category included Fake Fax Message, Fake Voice Message, Microsoft Password Expiration, Suspicious Account Activity, and Safe Account Notification. Each category had several samples that could be used to compare the differences between the phishing emails and safe emails.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (The second step was to analyze each email sample by reviewing the email header, subject, body, formatting, hyperlinks, attachments, and other elements. Each email was analyzed in terms of the presence of phishing indicators, such as sender address, subject line, message content, suspicious formatting, links, attachments, and other elements. Particular attention was paid to the sender address, subject line, and message content, as they normally indicate the presence of phishing attempts.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (The third step was to classify the email according to the detected phishing indicators and their impact on the business. The classification included the Phishing, Suspicious, and Safe categories. Each category was characterized by the presence of particular phishing indicators and their impact on the business if the email message was opened.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 170 0 R
/E (The final step was to prepare the phishing email detection report that included the screenshots of the email messages under analysis, email analysis results, phishing indicators, email classification, business impact, and the recommendations on phishing email prevention. The described methodology is based on ethical principles and allows detecting phishing email attempts by analyzing the email content and following the necessary safety precautions. The analysis of the sample emails demonstrated that the methodology can be used to increase cybersecurity awareness in the case of employees being able to analyze the emails and detect phishing attempts.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
