/P 171 0 R
/E (The phishing email detection and awareness assessment was performed using a specific procedure to ensure the accuracy of results. Initially, the email samples were selected from public sources as phishing, suspicious, and legitimate emails. All emails were examined in terms of sender, subject, content, links, attachments, and other elements. Different signs of phishing emails were detected and listed. Then, each email was categorized as phishing, suspicious, or safe based on the findings. The potential impact of each email type was defined, and the recommended prevention measures and user awareness considerations were determined. Following that, the assessment results were summarized in a phishing detection and awareness report along with relevant screenshots and other details.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
