/T (Other phishing indicators included generic greetings in the email body or requests for disclosing personal information, such as usernames and passwords, the presence of grammar or spelling mistakes, and the use of different domains not associated with the purported sender. Notably, legitimate companies use personalized communication with clients, refrain from asking for the disclosure of personal information, and do not contain multiple spelling or grammar mistakes. Based on the examination, it is important to note that not all suspicious emails are phishing attempts. Some emails addressed as spam or suspicious may involve legitimate activity, such as the given example in the suspicious email category, which did not contain any phishing indicators. At the same time, the examined legitimate email sample demonstrates no signs of phishing attempts, including the presence of a verified sender, clear objective of the message, and its absence of suspicious attachments or hyperlinks. Overall, the phishing indicators are crucial to ensure cybersecurity and protect users from phishing email scams. It is also vital for users to follow several essential guidelines to minimize the possibility of becoming a victim of cybercrime, such as double-checking the sender before responding or providing any information, avoiding clicking on any links and attachments in case of being suspicious. Furthermore, it is vital to report such cases to the relevant organizations to improve overall email security and address potential weaknesses.)
