413 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (Employees are the best defense mechanism in an organization against phishing and other email scams. Organizations have implemented technical controls to protect their systems, networks, and data. These include secure email servers, firewalls, anti-virus software, and multifactor authentication, among others. However, criminals are more likely to target the weakest link in the security chain, which is often the human factor. This is because most data breaches and cyber-attack incidents stem from human error. Thus, simply clicking on a spam link or opening an infected attachment can lead to password compromise and illegal access to confidential company information and finances.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
414 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 191 0 R
/E (The above facts highlight the need to increase employee cybersecurity awareness. Every staff member, including those untrained in IT, should learn how to identify spam emails and know what to do if they receive one. It is always advisable to be extra careful when dealing with emails requesting sensitive information. Being wary of such emails can prevent the organization from experiencing a huge financial and data disaster.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
