/P 193 0 R
/E (As a result, three email samples were detected as phishing, one suspicious, and one safe. The assessment helped compare the difference between phishing and safe emails, understand why some emails are labeled suspicious, and highlight that not every unsolicited email is dangerous. It was critical to ensure the security of the organization by double-checking every suspicious email and avoiding interactions with phishing emails. The assessment was also conducted to emphasize that even the most advanced and reliable security measures, including email filtering, antivirus, anti-malware, and multi-factor authentication, can be bypassed by social engineering.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
